# 0332i = 0332b + MS OS 1.0 (WCID) on bcdUSB 2.00, gated by rubywinusb=4
# (default 0; modes 1-3 keep the MS OS 2.0 semantics).  Windows PnP OK and
# WinUSB bound on the first single flash; 0xEE, compat ID (wIndex 4) and
# properties (wIndex 5) were verified end-to-end.  Mode 4 bumps bcdDevice
# 0x0211 -> 0x0212 so Windows re-probes 0xEE instead of using its cache.
#
# patchset 10b22c8f31b7bfd27cdc6e4613f57b2b4b5e04b647cbcfb53fde0f6196f5aadd
# (303 files; 0001-0079 baseline + project patches through 0332i)
# local VM kernel: full 985d97d9..., exec 382b835d... (includes private
# setup-dump diagnostics, so it is not the CI-tree kernel; record-only here)
# image: x16-0332i-ms10.img bf695e1a... (cmdline 587 B, rubywinusb=4)
#
# KERNEL_EXPECT_EXEC_DATA is empty for the first CI run: kernel_hash.py
# records the exec-data hash; pin it here after the run.
KERNEL_EXPECT_EXEC_DATA=